  "raw_text": "113\n\n(Note/Nota:\n \nku\n \nand\n \nkku\n \ncan be used as a suffix to indicate\n \nthrough\n \nor\n \nby way of\n \nthe noun it is added to. When the noun is plural,\nthe\n \nkku\n \nis added to the word\n \nnani\n \nthat follows.\n \n/\n \nku\n \ny\n \nkku\n \nse pueden usar como sufijo para indicar\n \na través del\n \nsustantivo al que\nse agrega.\n \nCuando el sustantivo es plural, el\n \nkku\n \nse agrega a la palabra\n \nnani\n \nque sigue.\n)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nbh\n-\n185\n):\n \nAni tnatka\n \nnanikku G\nâ\nd latwan wan kaiki ba marikisa ki?\n \n–\n \nThrough which ways does God show us love?\n \n/ ¿De\n\nqué maneras nos muestra Dios amor?)\n\nD\nî\nakku?\n \n–\n \nThrough what?\n \n/\n \n¿\nPor qu\né\n \ncosas\n?\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nwqu\n-\n07/21\n):\n \nGedeón ba diakku luan?\n \n–\n \nWhat did Gideon go through?\n \n/ ¿Por qué\n \ncosas\n \npasó\n \nGedeón\n?\n)\n\nPlenku\n \n–\n \nby plane\n \n/ en avión\n\nSakripaiskakku\n \n–\n \nthrough the sacrifice\n \n/ a través del sacrificio\n\nWalakku\n \n–\n \nthrough other, through another\n \n/ a través de otro\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nbh18\n):\n \nBaibil ra diara smalki ba, tnatka walakku sip lan takras\n \n–\n \nThings taught in the Bible are not able to be learned\nin other ways\n \n/ Las cosas que se enseñan en la Biblia no se pueden aprender de otras maneras)\n\nK\nû\na\n \n(1) (n/\ns)\n \n–\n \nbasket made from a tree called “sani”\n \n/ canasta hecha de un árbol llamado \"sani\"\n\n(Construct: _____;\n \nKwamya\n-db-Kli Smalkanka 26:4\n)\n\nK\nû\na\n \n(2) (n/s)\n \n–\n \nlouse\n \n/ piojo\n\nKuakaia\n \n–\n \nsee/ver:\n \nKwâkaia\n\nKuakua\n \n(\ndict, tc-Sandy Bay Sirpi\n)\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nbeetle\n \n/ escarabajo\n\nKuala\n \n–\n \nsee/ver:\n \nKwala\n\nKuawaia\n \n–\n \nsee\n/ver:\n \nKw\nâw\naia\n\nKubus\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nstove, oven\n \n/ estufa, horno\n\nKuhbaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto cough\n \n/ toser\n\nDusa kuhbaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto accuse\n \n/ acusar\n\nDusa kakuhbra\n \n(n\n-\nagent/s\n-\nagente)\n \n–\n \naccuser\n \n/ acusador\n\n(Note/Nota: Used at\n \ndb,dba,dbta-1 Korint 5:11\n \nto translate\n \nreviler.\n \nNot found in literature\n.\n \n/ Se usa en\n \ndb, dba,\n\ndbta\n-\n1\n \nKorint\n \n5:11\n \npara traducir\n \ninjuriador\n. No se encuentra en la literatura.)\n\nSiahka kuhbaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto cough because of a cold\n \n/ toser por un resfriado\n\nKuhma\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nthigh, leg, the\n \nentire\n \nleg\n \n/ muslo, pierna, toda la pierna\n\n(Construct:\n \nKuhmi\n \n–\n \nmy leg\n \n/ mi pierna\n;\n \nKuhmam\n \n–\n \nyour leg\n \n/ tu pierna\n;\n \nAi\n \nk\nuhma\n \n–\n \nhis/her/its/their\n \nleg\n \n/ su pierna\n)\n\nKuhma tâmaia\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nleg hair\n \n/ vello de la pierna\n\nKuk\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \ncook\n \n/ cocinero\n\nKuk takaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto cook\n \n/ cocinar\n\nKuka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \ngrandmother\n \n/ abuela\n \n(See also/ Ver también:\n \nDama\n \n–\n \ngrandfather\n \n/ abuelo)\n\n(Construct:\n \nKukiki\n;\n \nKukikam\n;\n \nKukika\n)\n\nKuka yaptika\n \n–\n \ngreat grandmother\n \n/ bisabuela\n\n(Construct:\n \nKukika yaptika\n)\n\nKukaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto gather, to accumulate, to treasure\n \n/ reunir, acumular, atesorar\n\nDiara kukanka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nsomething accumulated, something gathered\n \n/ algo acumulado, algo reunido\n\nKuki\n \n(1)\n \n–\n \nwith, united, together, in company of, along with, together with\n \n/ con, unidos, juntos, en compañía de,\njunto con\n \n(See also / Ver también:\n \nAikuki\n)\n\nKuki\n \n(2)\n \n–\n \n(v-continuous form of the verb\n \nKukaia\n \n/ forma continua del verbo\n \nKukaia\n)\n \n–\n \ngathering, accumulating,\ntreasuring\n \n/ reuniendo, acumulando, atesorando\n\nKukas\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nfly\n \n/ mosca\n\nKuku\n \n(a/t:\n \nKûku\n-\nay,db\n) (n/s)\n \n–\n \ncoconut\n \n/ coco\n\nKuku ailka\n \n–\n \ncoconut oil\n \n/ aceite de coco\n\nKuku dusa\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \ncoconut tree\n \n/ árbol de coco\n\nKuku laya\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \ncoconut water\n \n/ agua de coco\n\nKuku milk\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \ncoconut milk\n \n/ leche de coco\n\n(\nConstruct:\n \nKuku milkki\n;\n \nKuku milkkam\n;\n \nKuku milkka\n)\n\nKuku kura\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nyoung coconut\n \n/ coco joven\n\n(\nNote/Nota\n: S\nome just say\n \nKur\na\n \nto describe a young coconut\n \n/ Algunos solo dicen\n \nKura\n \npara describir un coco joven\n)\n\nKul\n \n–\n \nsee/ver:\n \nSkul",
